   "source": [
    "## Task 2: Data preparation\n",
    "- Split into features (z) and target (x)\n",
    "- Encode the target (good/bad -> 0/1)\n",
    "- Separate continuous vs categorical features\n",
    "- One-hot encode categoricals, standardize continuous\n",
    "- Recombine into one feature matrix z\n",
    "- Split into estimation (train) and test sets"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 25,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "['bad' 'good']\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "raw_target = credit_risk.iloc[:, -1]\n",
    "features = credit_risk.iloc[:, :-1]\n",
    "\n",
    "lb = LabelEncoder()\n",
    "target = lb.fit_transform(array(raw_target))\n",
    "print(lb.classes_)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "d4a83906",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "labelencoder to transform good/bad to 1/0"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "2f9319e6",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "That means class 1 = \"good\" — so from here on, \"predicted probability of class 1\" means \"probability this applicant is a good credit risk\", not a defaulter."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 31,
   "id": "d75cfe9e",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "i_cat, i_cont = [],[]\n",
    "for i, col in enumerate(features.columns):\n",
    "    i_cat.append(i) if features[col].dtype.name == 'category' else i_cont.append(i)\n",
    "\n",
    "features_cat_raw = features.iloc[:, i_cat]\n",
    "features_cont_raw = features.iloc[:, i_cont]"
   ]
  },
